{"name":"Compact Disc Grey","hex":"#cdcdcd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"compact","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An agreement or contract."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form an agreement or contract."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compact"},{"term":"disc","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thin, flat, circular plate or similar object.","An intervertebral disc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To harrow with a disc harrow.","To move towards, or operate at, zero blade pitch, orienting the propeller blades face-on to the oncoming airflow and maximizing the drag generated by the propeller."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disc"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Compact disc","blocks":[{"text":"The compact disc (CD) is a digital optical disc data storage format co-developed by Philips and Sony to store and play digital audio recordings. It employs the Compact Disc Digital Audio (CD-DA) standard and is capable of holding uncompressed stereo audio. First released in Japan in October 1982, the CD was the second optical disc format to reach the market, following the larger LaserDisc (LD). In later years, the technology was adapted for computer data storage as CD-ROM and subsequently expanded into various writable and multimedia formats. By 2007, over 200 billion CDs had been sold worldwide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Compact_Disc_wordmark.svg/330px-Compact_Disc_wordmark.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compact_disc","wikidata":"Q34467"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/CD_autolev_crop_new.jpg/500px-CD_autolev_crop_new.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/CD_autolev_crop_new.jpg/500px-CD_autolev_crop_new.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACD_autolev_crop_new.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Schouhamerimmink.jpg/330px-Schouhamerimmink.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Schouhamerimmink.jpg/330px-Schouhamerimmink.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dutch inventor and Philips chief engineer Kees Schouhamer Immink was part of the team that produced the standard compact disc in 1980","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASchouhamerimmink.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Sony-Discman-D-E307CK.jpg/500px-Sony-Discman-D-E307CK.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Sony-Discman-D-E307CK.jpg/500px-Sony-Discman-D-E307CK.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sony Discman D-E307CK portable CD player with 1-b